        "Foam is the primary comfort element in any upholstered sofa — the material that provides both the initial surface softness and the deeper structural support that keeps you correctly seated without contact with the frame below. All foam degrades over time under the combined effect of mechanical compression from use and environmental factors — principally moisture cycling and temperature variation. In Gurgaon's climate, these environmental factors are particularly aggressive: the AC season's 8–12 months of dry air at 20–30% humidity accelerates foam oxidation, and the monsoon's humidity spikes cause moisture absorption in open-cell foam structures that compounds the mechanical degradation from daily use.",
